This is a bug that is kind of related to #111916. It is an edge case that was not fixed by #111994 and actually came up in the PR. We parse two values for the same object mapper `second` (due to a higher-level array). First value is an array so `store_array_source` kicks in and stores the array `[ { "leaf": "hello1" } ]`. During second parsing pass, value is not an array, `store_array_source` does not kick in and we parse fields as usual. Later when synthetic source is constructed we see that there is an ignored source entry for this field. Since ignored source takes precedence over native impl, we only write that to source which results in lost data.

Repro (tests caught it with `dynamic: runtime` which has the same structure):
```
PUT /my_index
{
  "mappings": {
    "_source": { "mode": "synthetic" },
    "properties": {
      "top": {
        "properties": {
          "second": {
            "store_array_source": true,
            "properties": {
              "leaf": {
                "type": "keyword"
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

POST my_index/_bulk?refresh
{ "create": {} }
{ "top": [ { "second":[ { "leaf": "hello1" } ] }, { "second": { "leaf": "hello2" } } ] }

POST my_index/_search
```

Produces:
```
"_source": {
    "top": {
        "second": [
            {
                "leaf": "hello1"
            }
        ]
    }
}
```
